    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "<div class=\"description\">\n<table class=\"mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"clear:both;margin:2px auto;background:var(--background-color-base, #FFF);color:inherit;border:1px solid #AAA;padding:1px;width:100%\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"font-size:88%;background:var(--background-color-neutral, #eaecf0);border:none;color:inherit;padding:0 .2em;text-align:center\">Caption from the museum's website\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"mw-collapsible-content\" style=\"font-size:88%;border:none;padding:0;\">\n<p>Largely forgotten today, De Lairesse was celebrated in his lifetime as a painter and advocate for an idealizing manner based on the study of classical antiquity. This work, likely destined to hang over the mantelpiece in a grand Amsterdam home, depicts the sun god consorting with the goddess of the dawn, a popular subject in French and Italian painting at the time. The attractively individualized young faces have led to speculation that they may be disguised portraits of a newly married couple.\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
      "source": "commons-desc-page"
    },
